WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.468
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.803
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.405
[ Cheers and applause ]
Wow!

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.640
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.675
Well, guys,
this is very exciting.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:13.045
Today, New York ended its
pandemic state of emergency.

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:14.514
It's over.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.416
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.519
But, unfortunately,
that also means

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.621 line:0%
the end of to-go cocktails...

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.889 line:0%
[ Audience boos ]

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.391
...marking the first time

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.460
anyone's been nostalgic
for 2020.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.295
It's too bad.

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.964
I'm really gonna miss
seeing delivery guys

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.399
balance yardstick margaritas
on their E-bikes.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.334
Whoa-a-a-a.

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.470
Speaking of New York, the state

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.840
just suspended Rudy Giuliani
from practicing law

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.008
'cause of...

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.744
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.081 line:0%
...'cause of his repeated false
and misleading statements

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:50.950 line:0%
about the election.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.020
Even Rudy was like, "What
the hell took you so long?"

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.823
You know you've crossed a line
when other lawyers are like,

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.991
"This guy lies way too much."

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:00.994
It's a mixed bag for Rudy.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.962
The bad news -- he can't
practice law in New York.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.598
The good news -- he can't defend
himself at his next trial.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.269
Meanwhile, when the news
about Rudy broke,

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.938
his son Andrew
released a video statement.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.405
Watch this.

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:16.642
-As you may have heard recently,
a few minutes ago,

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:19.411
my father's law license
was suspended

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:20.880
by the New York state

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.583
First Appellate Division
of the Supreme Court.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:27.587
This is unacceptable,
and I stand by my father.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.990
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.259
[ Applause ]

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.430
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:44.270
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.807 line:0%
-The top 20% of his body
stands with his father.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:52.245
What did he use to film that?
A truck's rear-view camera?

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.247
Like, " Just put it in reverse
and hit 'record.'

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.783
Hey, I'll lay on the ground."

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.351
-[ Imitating backup signal ]

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:01.253
-Rudy saw his son giving
a speech in a random parking lot

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:03.189
and was like,
"I've taught him so well."

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.124
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.192
Some more legal news.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.027
A 49-year-old woman from Indiana

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.362
just became the first person
to be sentenced

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:12.197
for storming the Capitol,

00:02:12.197 --> 00:02:15.802 line:0%
receiving three years
of probation and a $500 fine.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.403
Yeah, the woman said
she learned her lesson

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:18.971
and hopes Trump pardons her

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:21.573
when he's reinstated
as President in August.

00:02:21.573 --> 00:02:23.743
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:27.646
Oh, my goodness.
Hey, here's some good news.

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:30.382
Today after meeting with
a bipartisan group of senators,

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:31.884
President Biden
finally announced

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.453 line:0%
that they had a deal
on infrastructure.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:36.889 line:0%
Yeah. right now,
New Yorkers are thinking,

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.058
"Okay, now, team up, and let's
save to-go cocktails.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.962
Let's go. That's the real --
Let's get to the -- Come on!"

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.464
[ Applause ]

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:48.367
That's right, Republicans and
Democrats working together --

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.069
amazing.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.437
It's like one of
those YouTube videos

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.139
of a lion making friends
with a squirrel.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.241
You know? It's possible.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.810
The compromise was actually
not that difficult.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.979
All it took was hard work,
determination,

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.115
and a blow dart
to Mitch McConnell's neck.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.983
[ Exhales sharply, groans ]

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.052
-"I've been hit."

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.954
-Well, the President
held a press conference

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.756
to discuss the big
infrastructure deal,

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.624
which brings us to
a new piece called

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.527
"Joe Biden, Whisperer-in-Chief."

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:18.064 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:21.033 line:0%
-And he said, "People
are waiting for relief."

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:26.739 line:0%
[Whispering ] I got them
$1.9 trillion of relief so far.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:31.376 line:0%
Just remind them, I wrote
the bill on the environment.

00:03:31.376 --> 00:03:33.846 line:0%
[ Normal voice ] When employers
can't find workers,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.749 line:0%
I said, "Yeah [whispering]
pay them more."

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.284
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.952
-What?!

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:41.955
-I love it.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.989
-Wow.

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:46.258
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:47.994
-He closed by saying
[whispering] "If you build it,

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.729
they will come."

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.364
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.498
[ Normal voice ] Well,
some business news.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.500
After disappointing sales,
Dunkin' Donuts

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.336
has pulled the Beyond Meat
breakfast sandwich

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:58.838
from their national menu.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.240
-Oh, come on!

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.574
-Yep. Dunkin' was shocked
plant-based foods

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:04.444
didn't appeal to
the same customers

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:07.080
who eat strawberry frosting
for breakfast.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.948
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.416
Some more business news.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.551
I read a headline today
that kind of confused me.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:17.089
It said, "T-Mobile released
its own 5G-inspired gin,"

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:19.792
which brings us to a segment
we like to call

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.661
"Uhh...I Have Some Questions."

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:26.532
-♪ I have some questions ♪

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:31.037 line:0%
-First up, why is a phone
company releasing its own gin?

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.404 line:0%
Actually, hold on.

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:35.408 line:0%
What does it mean
to be "5G-inspired"?

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.878 line:0%
Like, does the gin
taste like a 5G network?

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.446 line:0%
Wait, back up.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.882 line:0%
Where would I even buy
T-Mobile gin?

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.951 line:0%
Do I have to track down
a T-Mobile store,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:48.554 line:0%
and, if so, do they offer
unlimited gin plans?

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.390 line:0%
Follow-up -- Is it cheaper
if my whole family

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.492 line:0%
is on the same gin plan?

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.528 line:0%
But what if my wife
doesn't like gin?

00:04:56.528 --> 00:04:58.698 line:0%
What if my kids love gin?

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.232 line:0%
And again, what is
"5G-inspired"?

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:01.801 line:0%
I just have so many questions.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:07.206
-♪ I just have
so many questions ♪

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.741
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.142
-Oh, this is very interesting.

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:13.012
I saw that McDonald's is
phasing out its value meals...

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.246
-Aww.

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:17.282
-...and shifting towards
more expensive menu items.

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:18.985
It's already starting
to feel different.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.619
Just look at their
latest commercial.

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:22.821
-Delight your senses
at McDonald's.

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:26.159 line:0%
Partake in the Superior Mac
for $29.99.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:29.162 line:0%
Savor the Filet-Mignon-O-Fish
for $37.50.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.064 line:0%
Or indulge in
the golden crispiness

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:32.932 line:0%
of Sir Ronald McDonald's Nuggets

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.801 line:0%
with dipping sauces three --

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.570 line:0%
Black Truffle Caviar,
Sumptuous Fois Gras,

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.939 line:0%
and, of course, Honey Mustard.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:44.877 line:0%
McDonald's -- ba da ba ba ba --
I'm enamored with it.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.145 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.247 line:0%
-I'm enamored.
-I was enamored with it.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.815 line:0%
Wow.

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:52.885 line:0%
-And finally, a new survey found
that nearly half of American men

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:55.487 line:0%
experimented with their look
last year.

00:05:56.722 --> 00:05:58.724
Experimenting with your look
is one way of putting it.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.960
I mean, guys were cutting
their hair with nail clippers.

